# =============================================================================
# .bobignore — files and folders Bob must never read or edit
# =============================================================================
# Lives in the WORKSPACE ROOT (next to .git), not inside .bob/.
# Same pattern syntax as .gitignore:  dir/   *.ext   path/file   **/   !exception
#
# What it does
#   - Bob's file tools (read, write, apply_diff, insert, search) refuse matching files.
#   - Ignored files are hidden (or shown with a lock) in Bob's file listings.
#   - Common file-reading shell commands (cat, grep ...) on them are blocked.
#   - Bob reloads it automatically when you save, and can never edit it itself.
#
# What it does NOT do
#   - It does not stop YOU attaching a file with an @mention (@.env sends it anyway).
#   - It is not a sandbox: other shell commands can still touch these files.
#     Pair it with hooks (.bob/hooks/) and restricted modes for real protection.
#   - It only applies inside the current workspace.
#
# Docs:  https://bob.ibm.com/docs/ide/configuration/bobignore
# Guide: .bob/docs/02-agents-md-and-bobignore.md
# =============================================================================

# Credentials and connection details (keep .env.example readable as a template)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets/**

# Production data extracts and spooled output: may contain customer data
data/extracts/**
**/*.splf
**/spool/**
**/*.savf

# Bob's own runtime logs, written by the hooks
.bob/logs/**

# Caches and virtual environments: large and useless to Bob.
# (Build logs in .logs/ and .evfevent/ stay VISIBLE on purpose: the /build command
#  reads compile errors from them.)
**/__pycache__/**
**/.venv/**
node_modules/**
